    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "A\nPSA\n727-214\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION\nFOR OUR 727-214 FANJET PASSENGERS\nEven though you may be an experienced air traveler, there are certain\nfeatures of this, the most modern of air transports, with which you may\nnot be familiar.\nPACIFIC SOUTHWEST AIRLINES\nAUTOMATIC OXYGEN SYSTEM\nThe higher altitudes at which this aircraft operates require the\nprompt use of the automatic oxygen system in case of any\nsudden change in cabin pressure. Should a decompression occur\noxygen masks will drop down. Take nearest mask and promptly\nplace over nose and mouth. Adjust Headband: Breathe normally.\nNO SMOKING\n69\nFORWARD\nFACING\nSEAT\nBREATHE\nNORMALLY\nSEAT BELT\nEven if the \"SEAT BELT\" sign\nis turned off in flight, it is\nrecommended that you keep\nyour seat belt loosely fastened,\nwhenever you are in your seat.\nFLOTATION EQUIPMENT\nBRACING POSITION\nREAR\nFACING\nSEAT\nin\nthe\nevent of a water landing,\ncushion may be used as an aid\nto\nkeep afloat. Grasp the cushion at the\nrear, pull it forward and take it with\nyou.\nPlace arms through\nstraps on\nbottom to retain cushion.\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT\nSEE REVERSE SIDE\nPSA 17A\nRev. 6-21-68",
      "B\nWE SUGGEST THAT WHILE SEATED YOU\nKEEP YOUR SEAT BELT FASTENED\n727-214\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION\nFOR OUR 727-214 FANJET PASSENGERS\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nThere are nine exits provided for your use. The chart below will\nshow you the one closest to your seat. The exits over the wings\nare removable windows. The two exits forward and the two side\nexits aft are doors which are equipped with fast operating\nevacuation slides.\nFWD CABIN DOORS\nFWD\nENTRY\nDOOR (LH Side)\nAND\nFWD\nGALLEY\nDOOR (RH Side)\nROTATE\nHANDLE\nCLOSED\nOPEN\nPUSH\nDOOR\nOUT\nSLIDE\nWINDOW EXITS\nSTEP 1\nSTEP 2\nPULL\nDOWN\nTHIS\nFLAP\nGRASP\nHANDLE\nAND\nPULL\nDOWN\nPULL\nTOP\nINWARD\nAND\nLIFT\nAFT SERVICE DOORS\nAFT\nSERVICE\nDOOR\nOPEN\n(LH and RH Side)\nPULL\nOUT\nHANDLE\nAND\nROTATE 180°\nCLOSED\nPUSH\nSLIDE\nDOOR\nOUT\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nENTRY\nDOOR\nAND\nESCAPE\nSLIDE\nGALLEY\nSERVICE\nDOOR\nAND\nESCAPE\nSLIDE\nWINDOW\nEXITS\nTWINDOW\nEXITS\nSERVICE\nDOOR\nBAND\nESCAPE\nSLIDE\nSERVICE\nDOOR\n•AND\nTESCAPE\nSLIDE\nMAIN\nREAR\nCABIN\nDOOR\nPLACARDS GIVING\nSTEPS FOR OPERATION\nOF EVACUATION\nSLIDE\nARE LOCATED ON EACH\nDOOR. SLIDE IS SHOWN\nREADY FOR USE.\n=\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT\nSee Reverse Side\n2007.011.070"
    ],
